function infoCa_injectToCodex()
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addCategory', 'ca_cat', 'Cosmic Ascendancy'%_t, 'data/textures/icons/vortex.png')

    -- The Eclipse Crisis (Deep Dive)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c0', 'The Eclipse Crisis (Deep Dive)'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a0', 'Eclipse Faction Stats & Traits'%_t, 'Eclipse vessels are exceptionally deadly due to their specialized "Void Shields" and highly coordinated AI logic:\n- Void Shields: Incoming physical damage (Cannons, Bolters, Chainguns) is mitigated by 80%. You must use high-tier Energy/Antimatter/Plasma weapons to strip their shields.\n- Armor Plating: Base Hull HP is multiplied by 2.5x relative to vanilla generated ships of the same volume. Furthermore, all Eclipse blueprints have been upgraded to use Avorion (Tier 6) material blocks, granting them colossal base health pools.\n- Weaponry: The Eclipse exclusively utilize massive EMP lasers and high-velocity Plasma Artillery, making them incredibly lethal against your own shields.\n- Aesthetics & Classes: Eclipse ships are towering, jet-black monolithic structures accented by crimson energy fields. They fly Nullifiers (Pyramids), Obliterators (Monoliths), Harbingers (Obelisks), and 4 specialized combat classes: the Juggernaut (Dreadnought), Interceptor (Fighter), Harvester (Miner), and Defiler (Assault Frigate).\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a_abilities', 'Eclipse Combat Abilities'%_t, 'Eclipse ships wield devastating, class-specific mechanics to obliterate fleets:\n- Dark Matter Blink (All Ships): Upon taking 15% burst damage within 1 second, the ship will violently blink 5-10km away to escape, leaving behind a Void Rift (cooldown: 45s).\n- Ethereal Phase-Shift (Interceptors & Phantoms): Slippery vanguards instantly phase out of reality for 4 seconds upon shield break, becoming an invincible void-shadow to reposition and healing 25% of their shields.\n- Adaptive Resistance (Defilers & Artillery): These heavy combatants analyze incoming fire; taking 5% Hull/Shield damage from a specific element (e.g., Plasma) triggers a 15-second resistance to that element where they heal back 50% of the incoming damage!\n- Void Siphon Aura (Command Ships): Massive command ships constantly project a 10km devouring aura, rapidly draining the shield capacity of all nearby player ships to heal themselves for 25% of the drained amount.\n- Singularity Implosion (Capital Ships): Upon death, these gargantuan reactors collapse. After a 3-second warning, they violently detonate, stripping 15% of a player\'s Max Hull within 3km!\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a1', 'Invasion Mechanics & Threat Escalation'%_t, 'The Eclipse dynamically targets sectors containing high player or AI faction value.\n- Scouting Phase: Small, fast-moving Eclipse Interceptors will arrive in a sector. If they are not destroyed within 5 minutes, they broadcast a beacon.\n- Assault Phase: Once the beacon is active, a massive invasion fleet will warp in.\n  - Fleet Composition: 1 Dreadnought, 3 Cruisers, 5-8 Corvettes.\n- Eradication: Eclipse fleets prioritize destroying Stations. If they destroy an AI faction station, the sector\'s local economic output drops permanently. If they destroy a Player station, the player obviously loses that asset.\n- Personal Ambushes: The Eclipse actively hunts players. Every 25-45 minutes, there is a 40% chance that an elite Eclipse strike team will personally ambush the player\'s current sector.\n- Territorial Conquest: The Eclipse\'s first foothold always appears near the galactic core, then spreads outward toward the rim over time rather than in a random direction. Each conquered sector is either a Conquest (a contested siege, if Cosmic War is installed) or an outright Annihilation.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a2', 'Eclipse Citadels'%_t, 'When an invasion is overwhelmingly successful, the Eclipse will permanently occupy the sector and construct a Citadel.\n- The Lockdown Matrix: Citadels generate a sector-wide interdiction field. Ships cannot jump out of a Citadel sector unless the Citadel is destroyed.\n- Siege Mechanics: Citadels have 200,000,000 base HP (scaling with difficulty) and are surrounded by 4 orbital defense platforms. \n- Loot: Destroying a Citadel guarantees a drop of 1-3 Legendary subsystems and massive quantities of Avorion ore, alongside unique crafting materials for the Ascendancy Forge.\n- Suppression Field: Destroying a Citadel halts all Eclipse invasions galaxy-wide, for a base of 6 real-time hours plus 2 more hours for every 10 sectors the Eclipse currently own.\n- Territorial Liberation: The Citadel\'s own sector, plus any Eclipse-held territory within a 15-sector radius of it, is reclaimed outright, permanently rolling their frontier back rather than just buying time.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a7', 'The Dark Sector'%_t, 'Deep within the Galactic Core (Barrier), players may encounter Eclipse-controlled Dark Sectors.\n- Spawn: When jumping into completely un-generated space inside the core, there is a 20% risk of it transforming into a Dark Sector.\n- Hazard: The sector is engulfed in dense Dark Matter Fog and dominated by Eclipse Citadels guarded by Juggernaut dreadnoughts.\n- Reward: These sectors contain extremely dense Ascendant Matter and Ogonite asteroid fields, making them incredibly lucrative if you survive.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a6', 'The World Eater (Endgame Boss)'%_t, 'The World Eater is a 6-kilometer long Pyramid dreadnought built entirely of Avorion that spawns every 3-5 hours of active playtime (the timer pauses when no players are online).\n\n- Scales With Your Group: Its shields, hull, and damage grow for every extra defender present when it spawns, whether it warped in on its own or you summoned it yourself. A solo fight stays exactly as tuned; an alliance faces a genuinely tougher boss instead of trivializing it.\n- Invulnerability Tethers: At 50% and 25% Hull, it spawns Anchor Pylons and becomes immune to damage until they are destroyed.\n- Quantum EMP Hazard: Periodically targets a player with a massive cyan glow. After 3 seconds, an EMP erupts, instantly stripping 100% of their shields and inflicting 25% Max Hull damage.\n- Gravity Anomaly Hazard: Spawns a dark purple Black Hole that pulls ships in and inflicts 5% Max Hull damage per second!\n- World-Breaker Laser: An axial beam that locks the boss in place and fires a blast dealing 100% of Max Shields + 50% of Max Hull.\n\nThe 6-Phase Gauntlet: As its hull is chipped away, the World-Eater triggers escalating desperation mechanics:\n\n- 80% HP: Summons 5 Defiler escorts.\n- 70% HP: Emits a global EMP pulse, instantly stripping 50% shield capacity from every ship and station in the sector.\n- 60% HP: Deploys additional Eclipse escorts to reinforce itself.\n- 50% HP: Initiates emergency repairs, violently blinking away and healing part of its colossal Max Hull.\n- 35% HP: Unleashes a second global EMP and enters an Enraged state (+50% Fire Rate, +50% Global Damage, projects a Dark Matter Aura).\n\nThe Stakes: If the World-Eater is not destroyed within 20 minutes, the sector is completely wiped and ownership transfers to the Eclipse. Destroying it (or surviving the wipe) grants the galaxy a 10-hour Grace Period where the Doomsday clock is paused entirely.\n\n- Raid Summoning: Jettisoning an Eclipse Datacore from your cargo hold tears open a hyperspace rift and instantly summons the World-Eater to your location!\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a9', 'The Fallen Empire Awakening'%_t, 'The Eclipse evolves into a Fallen Empire after conquering or annihilating 75 sectors unchecked.\n- Crusaders: The Eclipse deploy ultra-heavy Crusade fleets to systematically hunt down and wipe out AI Faction Capitals.\n- Player & Alliance Hunting: A Fallen Empire will also occasionally target a player\'s or alliance\'s own sectors, as long as there\'s a station on it, on a much slower cooldown than their AI-faction Crusades so it cannot camp the same target back to back. Losing a targeted sector this way never destroys your stations outright; the worst case is the sector turning hostile until you clear it back out.\n- Dark Matter Fog: Sectors captured by the Eclipse become veiled in Dark Matter Fog, imposing harsh debuffs to sensors and jump drives.\n- Weather Immunity: Awakened Eclipse ships are immune to all hazard weather effects.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a19', 'Remnant Escalation'%_t, 'A galaxy that keeps clearing World-Eaters and Citadels does not stay at the same difficulty forever.\n- Escalating Threat: Every confirmed kill builds toward a Remnant Tier, up to Tier 5 (a World-Eater kill counts for three times a Citadel kill). Each tier adds a modest Shield, Hull, and Damage bump to every future World-Eater and Citadel.\n- Shorter Fuse: Each tier also shrinks the World-Eater\'s 3-5 hour spawn window, by up to 75 minutes at the maximum tier.\n- Galaxy-Wide Warning: Escalating a tier is announced galaxy-wide and via the Galactic News Network. Check /eclipsestatus for your current tier and confirmed kill counts.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a10', 'Defeating Nemeses & Damage Gates'%_t, 'Elite Eclipse combatants, known as Nemeses, employ extreme survivability tactics:\n- Damage Gates: Nemesis shields and hulls cannot take more than 8% of their maximum health as damage per tick, preventing one-shot mechanics.\n- Elemental Resistances: Nemeses can dynamically adapt their hull plating to resist specific damage types that they have recently received.\n- Hunt the Dread-Lord: A retreating Nemesis relocates to a nearby sector to recover, healed back to a meaningful fraction of its Hull, instead of vanishing outright. The moment any player enters that sector, the wounded Dread-Lord materializes there, ready for a rematch. Destroying it this time pays out a bounty. Check /eclipsestatus for its last known coordinates.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a15', 'Adaptive Eclipse Scaling'%_t, 'The Eclipse adapts to the server\'s overall power level rather than staying static. The engine scans for the player with the highest Global Ascendancy Tier, and for each tier that player has achieved, the entire Eclipse faction globally receives a +50% multiplier to their physical ship volume, hull, and shields (capped at a 3.0x multiplier).\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Forging Ascendant gear and raising your Global Ascendancy Tier makes you personally stronger, but it also raises the stakes for the rest of the galaxy by making every Eclipse ship a tougher opponent.\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendant Campaign
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c4', 'The Ascendant Campaign'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c4', 'ca_cat_a14', 'Aegis, The Ascendant Envoy'%_t, 'Upon defeating the Wormhole Guardian and unleashing The Eclipse, you will be physically intercepted by Aegis, an ancient AI construct designed by the creators of the dimensional prison.\n\n- Physical Rendezvous: Instead of receiving basic radio messages, Aegis will transmit secure rendezvous coordinates to you. You must physically fly to these sectors to meet her projection.\n- 5-Part Storyline: She will guide you through a fully-scripted 5-mission campaign detailing the origins of The Eclipse, the location of the Ascendancy Forge, and the incoming World-Eater.\n- Massive Rewards: Returning to Aegis for a debrief injects massive credit payouts (scaling up to 25 Million) and high-tier equipment drops directly into your cargo hold.\n- Multiplayer Support: If you are playing with an alliance, Aegis will patiently remain stationed at the rendezvous point until all players in the sector have had a chance to speak with her and claim their own personal rewards!\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendancy Beacon
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c1', 'The Ascendancy Beacon'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c1', 'ca_cat_a3', 'Ascendancy Beacon Functionality'%_t, 'Players can construct the ultimate megastructure: The Ascendancy Beacon.\n\n- Permanent Sector Simulation: A sector containing an active Ascendancy Beacon is simulated 24/7, even if no players are online.\n- Global Buffs: The beacon applies a permanent, massive stat multiplier to all ships in the player\'s fleet across the entire galaxy.\n- Upgrades: The beacon can be upgraded through 5 tiers, exponentially increasing the global stat buffs but requiring massive, continuous upkeep costs of Credits, Avorion, and Ogonite.\n- Sanctuary Field (Tier 3+): Upgrading to Tier 3 or higher activates a field that actively repels Eclipse conquest and annihilation attempts within a radius of it, from 5 sectors at Tier 3 up to 12 at Tier 5. It stays active for as long as the Beacon does, even while its sector is unloaded.\n- The Grand Toll & Treasury Payouts: The beacon acts as an intergalactic border checkpoint. All NPC traders and AI factions jumping into the sector are charged a massive entry tax. The Beacon safely stores all collected tolls in its internal treasury and pays out a single lump-sum to your faction every 45 minutes.\n- Dynamic Wartime Premium: AI factions currently engaged in massive wars (Cosmic War integration) will desperately pay up to a +50% Premium Toll for seeking safe harbor in your heavily defended capital sector!\n- Capital Sieges: A hidden playtime clock runs within the beacon. Every 3 to 6 hours, a devastating siege fleet (Pirates, Xsotan, or War Factions) will invade your sector to destroy the beacon. If you defend it, you earn legendary loot. If it falls, your global buffs collapse.\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendancy Forge (Crafting & Math)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c2', 'The Ascendancy Forge (Crafting & Math)'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a4', 'Unlock Requirements'%_t, 'To combat the Eclipse, players must locate and utilize the Ascendancy Forge to craft gear that pushes past Avorion\'s native limits.\n\n- The Forge is discovered during "Forging the Defense," the second stage of the Ascendant Campaign.\n- Access is unlocked by feeding it an Eclipse Datacore via the "Decrypt Eclipse Datacore" option, salvaged from destroyed Eclipse vessels.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a5', 'Crafting Formula & Sacrifice Mechanics'%_t, 'Crafting Ascendant-tier gear at the Stellar Forge is extraordinarily expensive to balance its extreme power, and takes a full 24 real-time hours to complete.\n\n- Scaling Cost: Base cost is 50,000,000 Credits plus a full spread of raw ores (Iron through Avorion) and 25-50 Ascendant Matter. The closer your Forge is to the Galactic Core, the more expensive it gets, scaling all the way up to 300,000,000 Credits and 3,000,000 Avorion at the very center.\n- The Sacrifice System: When initiating a craft, the Forge requires a Catalyst. Sacrificing a Legendary subsystem grants +20% success rate, while an Exotic grants +10%.\n  - Ascendant Scrap: Any shortfall to 100% is automatically bridged by consuming Ascendant Scrap from your cargo hold, with each unit adding +2%.\n  - Failure: If the craft fails, all sacrificed subsystems and consumed materials are lost, but you are compensated with a batch of Ascendant Scrap to improve your next attempt.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a8', 'Titan Weaponry & Cybernetics'%_t, 'The Forge is capable of synthesizing incredibly complex superweapons and biological augmentations.\n\n- Ascendant World-Breaker (Titan Coaxial): A gargantuan, dreadnought-class axial beam laser dealing 250,000 continuous damage. Firing this weapon locks the ship\'s rotation.\n- Ascendant Neural Implant: A terrifying fusion of Eclipse technology and human neuro-links. This equippable ship subsystem massively augments the ship\'s captain, scaling up fighter control, jump reach, velocity, and weapons.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a16', 'Ascendant Relic Subsystems'%_t, 'Beyond the Neural Implant and World-Breaker, the Forge can synthesize a full family of "Living Relic" subsystems, each dramatically boosting a different ship role. All of them scale dynamically stronger the closer you fly to the Galactic Core and the higher local War Heat is.\n\n- Ascendant Slipstream Core: Massive boosts to velocity, jump reach, and hyperspace cooldown.\n- Ascendant War-Drive: Adds bonus turret slots, energy generation, and fire rate.\n- Ascendant Aegis Matrix: Enormous boosts to shield durability and recharge rate.\n- Ascendant Swarm Nexus: Boosts fighter squadron capacity, pilot count, and factory production speed.\n- Ascendant Void-Drill: Extends loot and transporter range alongside energy generation.\n- Ascendant Omni-Sensor: Boosts radar reach, reveals hidden sectors, and massively expands cargo hold and loot collection range.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a11', 'Factory Overdrive & Forge Decryption'%_t, 'Players can overclock their player-owned stations and their entire fleet through the Forge.\n\n- Factory Overdrive: By feeding 50 Ascendant Matter into the Forge, players can initiate a Factory Overdrive. All player stations will experience a 300% production speed boost for 1 real-time hour.\n- Forge Decryption Matrix: The Ascendancy Forge now accepts Eclipse Datacores. Decrypting them permanently raises your Global Ascendancy Tier, granting +15% Shields, +20% Shield Regen, and +10% Hyperspace Cooldown natively to all player ships.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a12', 'Automating Defense'%_t, 'Ascendant Gateways can be constructed to establish automated defense perimeters.\n- Function: Every 5 seconds, a Gateway scans its sector for hostile ships. When one is detected and its 2-hour cooldown has elapsed, it instantly warps in 3 Ascendant Guardian defenders to hold the line.\n'%_t, '')

    -- Dynamic Faction Expansion
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c5', 'Dynamic Faction Expansion'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c5', 'ca_cat_a17', 'Living Borders'%_t, 'Vanilla Avorion features a static map. With Cosmic Ascendancy, civilized AI factions and Pirates will slowly and naturally expand their borders over time.\n\n- Organic Growth: Civilized factions trace outward from their home sectors to claim contiguous empty sectors, spawning new space stations and officially annexing the territory.\n- Pirate Bases: Deep space is no longer permanently safe. Pirates will occasionally establish Smuggler\'s Hideouts and Pirate Shipyards in completely uncharted systems.\n- News Alerts: All major territorial expansions are broadcast live via the Cosmic Chronicles News Network.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c5', 'ca_cat_a18', 'Player Commands'%_t, 'Cosmic Ascendancy provides a global chat command that any player, not just admins, can use to track the status of the Eclipse Crisis.\n\n/eclipsestatus: Privately outputs a full status report on the Eclipse Crisis:\n- Citadel Suppression Field: How much time is left on the invasion suppression caused by destroying an Eclipse Citadel.\n- World-Eater Grace Period: How much time remains on the 10-hour Doomsday pause after a World-Eater event.\n- Eclipse Holdings & Expansion Threat: Total sectors conquered or annihilated, and how close the Eclipse is to their next expansion attempt.\n- Fallen Empire Status: Whether the Eclipse has become a Fallen Empire, and their last Crusade target if so.\n- Nemesis Signature: The last known coordinates of a currently-fleeing, wounded Eclipse Dread-Lord, if one exists.\n- Remnant Escalation: The current Remnant Tier and confirmed World-Eater/Citadel kill counts.\n'%_t, '')

    -- Synergies & Integrations
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c3', 'Synergies & Integrations'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c3', 'ca_cat_a13', 'Cosmic Vault Synergy'%_t, 'Ascendancy utilizes several shared APIs provided by Cosmic Vault:\n- Eclipse Contraband: Illegal Ascendant tech can be fenced in Vault smuggling rings.\n- Dead Empire Filter: Vault Faction Index API tracks fallen empires and assigns them Eclipse Citadel conquer priority.\n- Relentless Expansion: Vault Territory API expands Eclipse borders naturally across the map.\n- Rift Spillage: Corrupted nodes spawn strange anomalies (via Vault Anomalies API).\n- Hazard Immunity: Eclipse ships utilize the Vault Buff API for weather immunities.\n- Post-Boss Anomalies: The destruction of a Citadel spawns exotic Vault-tracked anomalies for players to research.\n'%_t, '')
end
